question:
Find the number of ways to choose three points $A$, $B$, and $C$ on the geoboard such that triangle $ABC$ is a right triangle with a side length of 2 units and a hypotenuse that is not parallel to any side of the geoboard. [asy]
draw((0,0)--(0,6)--(6,6)--(6,0)--cycle,linewidth(1));
for(int i=1;i<6;++i)
{for(int j=1;j<6;++j)
{dot((i,j));}
}
[/asy]

The number $a_n$ is defined as the sum of the absolute values of the entries in the $n$th row of a modified Pascal's triangle where each entry is the difference between the corresponding entries of the original Pascal's triangle and its reflection across the vertical axis of symmetry. For example, the first few rows of the modified Pascal's triangle are:

\begin{tabular}{rccccccccc}
$n=0$:& & & & & 0\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
$n=1$:& & & & -1 & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
$n=2$:& & & -1 & & 0 & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
$n=3$:& & -1 & & -1 & & 1 & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
$n=4$:& -1 & & -2 & & 0 & & 2 & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
& & & & & $\vdots$ & & & &

\end{tabular}

Express $\frac{\log_{10} a_n}{\log_{10} 2}$ in terms of $n$.
